{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S2d PS5 (4129362c0d): root-caused py3.13 gen_cli_help --check staleness to TWO argparse-3.13 rendering changes. (1) _format_action_invocation now prints '-o, --output X' (metavar once) vs pre-3.13 '-o X, --output X' (per option string) -> 23 option-bearing core artifacts stale. (2) new _get_actions_usage_parts keeps subparsers '{choices} ...' as ONE usage part vs pre-3.13 regex-splitting it, so '...' no longer wraps -> bridge.txt stale. Fix: pinned both pre-3.13 renderings via overrides in RebarHelpFormatter (_format_action_invocation verbatim body; _get_actions_usage_parts re-splits with the historical regex, inert on <=3.12), and switched bridge's factory from stock argparse.HelpFormatter to RebarHelpFormatter (only advanced parser whose subparsers usage wraps). Verified on a real py3.13.5 interpreter: gen --check rc=0 on BOTH 3.12 and 3.13, artifacts byte-identical. Added 2 teeth tests (metavar-repetition + ellipsis-wrap) that hold on 3.12/3.13 and fail on stock 3.13. lint+typecheck+complexity(new=0)+module-size clean; parser/gen/b8de/advanced 58 passed; held-out 13/13. 26 *_heldout failures are the known host-only safe.bareRepository issue, not CI. Pushed PS5; both bots re-triggered."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787290287578607001,"uuid":"4e98df7d-7c58-43c5-bac2-b77e2a5ab84f"}